## Field Reference

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| `schema_version` | `"1"` | Yes | Domain-layer schema version |
| `subject` | string | Yes | What was analyzed |
| `task_resolution` | object | quick+ | Task/context resolution block (see below) |
| `domain_model` | object | standard+ | Concept map (omitted entirely in quick mode) |
| `findings[]` | array | Yes | Structured findings |
| `patterns[]` | array | standard+ | Pattern records (omitted entirely in quick mode) |
| `blind_spot_candidates[]` | array | Yes | Self-audit gap candidates |
| `scope` | object | Yes | What was and was not inspected |

### Finding fields

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| `id` | `FIND-NNN` | Yes | Unique finding id |
| `statement` | string | Yes | The finding, stated plainly |
| `category_path` | string | Yes | 1–4 dot-separated segments, `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{2,60}` each |
| `layer` | `L1–L4` | Yes | Abstraction layer (same scale as the rest of the skill) |
| `evidence_status` | enum | Yes | See status semantics below |
| `source_refs` | array | Yes | Real references; may be empty **only** with `evidence_scope` |
| `confidence_band` | `HIGH\|MEDIUM\|LOW` | Yes | Qualitative band (measurement split, §2) |
| `uncertainty_reason` | string | non-OBSERVED | Why the status is not OBSERVED |
| `evidence_scope` | string | empty refs | Where was searched — a null search confirms nothing beyond its scope |
| `verification_status` | `NOT_RUN\|RUN` | optional | Whether the finding's verification actually executed |
| `verification_evidence` | array | VERIFIED patterns | Commands/tool output cited when a check actually ran |

### Pattern fields

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| `id` | `PAT-NNN` | Yes | Unique pattern id |
| `member_finding_ids` | array | Yes | Findings supporting the pattern (must resolve) |
| `status` | `VERIFIED\|PROBABLE\|CANDIDATE` | Yes | Gated: VERIFIED needs ≥2 distinct sources **and** `verification_status: "RUN"` with cited `verification_evidence`; PROBABLE needs ≥1 source; otherwise CANDIDATE |
| `independence.distinct_sources` | int | Yes | Unique sources after content dedupe — repeated copies count once |
| `lexical_signal` | object | CLI-nominated | Present when the candidate came from lexical nomination (never a promoted status) |

### Blind-spot candidate fields

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| `id` | `BSX-NNN` | Yes | Unique candidate id |
| `description` | string | Yes | The gap |
| `why_it_matters` | string | Yes | Which result it could change — never name a gap without this |
| `smallest_useful_check` | string | Yes | The cheapest check that would settle it |

## Evidence Status Semantics

| Status | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| `OBSERVED` | Directly seen this session — cited tool output (commands, file reads, real paths) |
| `CANDIDATE` | Lexical/heuristic nomination — a signal to investigate, never a finding of fact |
| `INFERRED` | Agent reasoning from cited evidence — requires `uncertainty_reason` and a recorded reasoning chain |
| `HYPOTHESIS` | Explicitly unverified proposal — requires `uncertainty_reason` |
| `UNVERIFIED_CLAIM` | Asserted without evidence — requires `uncertainty_reason`; never phrase as confirmed |

**Honesty bounds:** heuristics nominate, agents decide with cited evidence. A check that never ran cannot back a `VERIFIED` claim — `verification_status` defaults to `NOT_RUN` and the validator rejects VERIFIED without `RUN` + cited evidence. Copies of identical content are one source, not independent evidence. A single occurrence is never a recurring-pattern conclusion.

